    description: "Nod Makerspace is a dynamic coworking and fabrication ecosystem set across the first and second floors of a converted industrial building in the Industria Bumbacului complex on Splaiul Unirii, in Bucharest's Sector 4. It welcomes designers, architects, artists, engineers, freelancers and entrepreneurs into a community of over 100 members.\n\nThe space is organised into three distinct coworking zones: The Quiet (a peaceful library section), The Casual (a relaxed first-floor environment for desk-based professionals) and The Active (a second-floor area integrated with the maker workshops). Members can choose flexible hot desks, dedicated desks, or private studios sized for teams of 2 to 15 people.\n\nBeyond the desks, Nod offers high-speed Wi-Fi throughout, meeting rooms, phone booths, a nap and meditation room, a cosy kitchenette with free coffee and tea, a materials library, and access to wood, metal and electronics workshops for rapid prototyping. A rooftop gastrobar and outdoor terrace round out the experience.\n\nMembership ranges from an entry day pass to a flexi 15-days-per-month plan and full-time 24/7 access, with digital nomad packages that include business registration services.",
